<SiteLayout title="Product direction — Retail POS Mobile" description="Learn the goals and current development status of Retail POS Mobile, an independent Android-first retail POS in foundation development." path="/product/">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><div class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Product</div><span class="eyebrow">Product overview</span><h1>One retail product. A deliberate foundation.</h1><p>Retail POS Mobile is being developed as an independent Android-first POS for everyday retail work. The current stage is foundation development; operational workflows are not yet available as a public release.</p><div class="status-line"><span class="status-pill status-foundation"><span class="status-dot"></span> Foundation development</span><span class="status-pill status-unavailable"><span class="status-dot"></span> No public APK</span></div></div></section>
<section class="content-section"><div class="container content-wrap">
<div class="notice"><span class="notice-icon" aria-hidden="true">i</span><div><strong>What this page means</strong><p>This is a description of product direction, not a claim that checkout, inventory, reporting, or offline transactions are currently available.</p></div></div>
<h2>Designed for real retail conditions</h2><p>The intended audience includes small retailers who need clear day-to-day records, a fast counter workflow, and an honest account of what happens when connectivity is unreliable. PKR and local shop workflows are part of the product context; exact payment, rounding, and reporting behavior will be documented after implementation and testing.</p>
<h2>Built as an independent product</h2><p>The mobile project defines a separate application and data boundary. It is not intended to reuse another POS product's database, authentication, APIs, storage, credentials, or runtime services.</p>
<h2>What guides the work</h2><div class="content-grid"><article class="content-card"><h3>Clarity at the counter</h3><p>Keep the selling flow focused and make important outcomes easy to understand.</p></article><article class="content-card"><h3>Traceable operations</h3><p>Design transaction and stock history so managers can investigate changes rather than guess.</p></article><article class="content-card"><h3>Safe retries</h3><p>Plan idempotent operations and durable sync behavior before treating offline selling as reliable.</p></article><article class="content-card"><h3>Honest availability</h3><p>Publish a feature as available only after implementation and relevant tests have been checked.</p></article></div>
<h2>What happens next?</h2><p>The foundation is being established first. As workflows become implemented and verified, feature status, release history, and download instructions will be updated together.</p><p><a class="text-link" href="/features/">Read the planned feature scope <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></p>
</div></section></SiteLayout>
